r granny vegar  slowly moving around given how massive  she is which they also did a good job in  communicating the skill of the dragons  like eamon's having to climb up vegar  like she was a tower or whenever they  positioned a dragon near one of our main  characters as a size comparison they do  not shy away from showing off their  dragons and that's also a refreshing  aspect because you can fully see them in  any night scene generally when VFX is  done at night it's always intentionally  done to hide the VFX but during vegar's  2 flight scenes you can clearly see  what's going on and since they don't  hide anything it makes for some insanely  good scenes veigar's last scene in the  finale because of this was easily one of  the best from how terrifying and scary  it was truly a very immersive experience  then that's just the visual side of  things because Ramin jawadi is back for  the score the man is still killing it  and the new themes he created for the  Valerian zornera were so good the chorus  chance of our nearest theme immediately  gives you this uplifted feeling that is  so addictive to listen to I also love  how it all culminates in her ending  scene when she becomes Queen in the  track called the crown of jaharis I  definitely recommend checking it out  along with the power of Prophecy then  the valerion theme sounds so unique with  its tribal-like Woodwinds playing with  drums and violins accompanying it it's  so fresh and distinct that it makes me  crave to see where mean jawadi flex and  experiment more within Westeros and  since we are on the subject of themes  it's kind of disappointing that there  wasn't a new main theme for House of the  dragon and they instead of used the one  from Game of Thrones it would make the  most sense to me to combine the themes  of near and House Targaryen for the  title sequence but oh well I think this  sets more of a lazy precedence for other  spin-off shows that are in development  and hope they don't follow down the same  path because it would be weird to hear  the same Game of Thrones theme in every  single show especially since the  upcoming sea snakes show as an example  already has such a cool theme but yeah  since the budget for House of the Dragon  is so big the production value of this  season is able to ascend and the result  is truly amazing so after going through  all of these scintillating positives  let's talk about some of the negatives  that bring the show down a little bit  starting with the pace at which the  story moves not in the sense of how  quickly each scene plays out because if  anything the writers take their time on  a scene to scene basis but more of the  fact of how fast time moves between  episodes AKA time jumps now it's really  hard to avoid this fact given that the  writers have to cover about 20 to 30  years of time within 10 episodes  personally I think it would have made  more sense to do a longer season so they  didn't have to skip so much time and  avoid that jarring feeling of having to  restart the show again I think Lancel  needs to get the shore Runners the  season stretcher because the main issue  with doing these time jumps is firstly  you are skipping over a lot of plot  lines my biggest gripe is getting thrown  into these developments at the mid  endpoint and we didn't get any build up  for them the worst examples of this is  her Harwin Strong's relationship with  rhaenyra and Damon's relationship with  Lena valerion within episode 6 both sir  Harwin and Elena die and you don't feel  that sad for them because there was no  time to build an emotional attachment to  these characters the whole point of  build up is to make us care about them  and understand who they are so when he  don't include it and throw their death  at us suddenly then we're going to feel  detached and the death has a soft impact  that and it's also just confusing to see  a character go from killing their wife  to them being in a family with a bunch  of kids in the next episode so having to  essentially re-meet these characters and  have to be introduced to what is  happening again shouldn't be the aim of  the writers and instead naturally get to  that point by taking more time to tell  your story then there's also the aspect  of how old the actors look now to me I  don't really care about this aspect that  much but it does become visually  confusing when someone like Kristen Cole  doesn't age at all within the 20 plus  years the show takes place in comparison  to other characters who age a lot like  hell the character Eamonn gets born in  between episodes five and six and he  looks just as old and if not older than  Kristin Cole by episode 8. So to that  degree it feels a bit inconsistent in  terms of how they age up the actors but  you kind of just have to accept that  aspect of the show because the only  option they have is to constantly keep  changing to older actors or use makeup  which using makeup I don't think would  really work so to change the actors  every 10 years within the show would be  even more jarring than just having the  same one to me the fans were already  losing their minds when they swapped out  Millie and Emily for their older  counterparts so doing that more  frequently I think would be much more  annoying so I think this just comes down  to people having to accept that part of  the show since there isn't a better  alternative to take for the last flaw of  the Season there are a couple of big  changes the writers make within the  story that I think needed to be  Rewritten or needed some time to breathe  the first example of this is Kristen  Cole's snapping and killing Joffrey the  reason why this development doesn't work  well is that they immediately do a  massive time Jump after it happens so  any big questions relating to this event  are instantly disregarded and aren't  addressed again like will there be any  repercussions for Kristen Cole doing  this does Allison defend him from being  kicked o